      {
        "id": 250829,
        "name": "OddballPaladin",
        "username": "OddballPaladin",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/o/d26b3c/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2023-02-16T19:23:03.116Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Joking aside, I could see some story potential in what Apostate did. Think of it this way, what if he decided to break up Dark Watch intentionally because of how fun watching the Prime Wardens implode was? So, to get inside, he had to create an alternate identity, that was strong enough to not immediately trigger whatever wards Nightmist and Harpy have around themselves. So everything about “Matthew” was completely genuine, but it was also a mask.</p>\n<p>This leads to an interesting look at nature vs nurture, because in the end, he had a choice, and chose nature, chose deception.</p>",
        "post_number": 27,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2023-02-16T19:23:03.116Z",
